  "title": "How MiniSearch works",
  "summary": "The browser sends the query to the app server, which asks the bundled SearXNG instance for results, reranks them with a small cross-encoder, and returns them for the browser to cache. With AI responses on, the browser then has a model write a cited answer from the top results, either in the browser or through a remote backend.",
